---
import PostLayout from "../layouts/PostLayout.astro";
---

<PostLayout
	title="Colophon"
	description="How this site is built."
	metadata={false}
>
	<p>
		Site powered by <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>.
	</p>

	<p>
		The style is a never-ending cycle of change that always ends up in
		frustration. Currently, it's stolen from <a href="https://mattwidmann.net"
			>mattwidmann.net</a
		>, which I apologize for. With my lack of design skills, I might resort to
		contracting a designer to help out.
	</p>

	<p>
		I write plain CSS with no preprocessor, kept as simple as I can manage so I
		don't get lost in a single massive stylesheet.
	</p>

	<p>
		Haven't dedicated much effort to make the site accessible, but throughout
		the coding process I tried to do as much as possible.
	</p>

	<p>
		The website does use JavaScript but works just fine without it for all the
		JS-free folks. You'll be able to read all the content, but certain
		JS-powered features will either be invisible or unavailable.
	</p>

	<p>It doesn't depend on resources from other domains.</p>
</PostLayout>
